==Arabic==

===Etymology 1===
From the root {{ar-root|م|س|ك}}.

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I|a|u,i}}

# to [[grab]], [[grasp]], [[clutch]], [[clasp]], [[seize]], [[take hold]]
# to [[hold]]
# to [[stick]], [[cling]], [[adhere]], [[hang on]]
<!-- Evidently only in particular expressions
# to [[keep]] ''(the books, accounts, etc.)''
# to [[take]] ''(charge, control, etc.)''
-->

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I|a|u,i|passive=y|vn=مَسْكٌ}}

=====References=====
* {{R:ar:Wehr}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|II}}

# to have someone [[seize]] or [[hold]] something

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|II}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|مَسْك|m}}

# {{ar-verbal noun of|مَسَكَ|form=I}}
# [[seizure]], [[grip]], [[hold]]
# [[keeping]] ''(bookkeeping, etc.)''

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|مَسْك}}

====Adjective====
{{ar-adj|مُسُك|f=مُسُكَة|pl=مُسَكَة}}

# [[grasping]], [[greedy]], [[avaricious]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-adj|مُسُك|pl=مُسَكَة}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{etyl|fa|ar}} {{term|مشک|tr=mošk|lang=fa||musk}}, from {{etyl|pal|ar}} {{term|𐭬𐭥𐭱𐭪𐭩|tr=mušk|lang=pal||musk}}.

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|II}}

# to [[scent]] with [[musk]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|II}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|مِسْك|m|g2=f}}

# [[musk]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|مِسْك}}

